# MIMIC-IV data — NEVER commit (PhysioNet DUA prohibits redistribution)
# NOTE: patterns are specific so they do NOT match the mimic_pipeline/ code dir
#       (macOS filesystem is case-insensitive).
mimiciv/
mimic-iv/
mimic_iv/
physionet.org/
# `data/` is excluded file-by-file rather than as a directory: git will not
# re-include anything inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so a blanket `data/` makes
# the PROVENANCE.md exception below unreachable. Matching contents keeps the
# exclusion and lets the prose through.
data/**
!data/
**/data/**
!**/data/
*.csv
*.csv.gz
*.parquet
*.feather
*.db
*.sqlite

# ...but keep provenance documents. These are prose (checksums, mirror URLs,
# column semantics, caveats) and carry no data rows. Without this exception the
# broad `data/` rule above silently swallows them, and a data file with no
# recorded provenance is worse than no data file.
!**/data/PROVENANCE.md
!**/PROVENANCE.md

# Recruitment logistics — OURS, not the paper's. Email drafts carry author names,
# institution and deadlines, so they would both break double-blind review and
# publish material no reader needs. The adjudication PROTOCOL is a different thing
# and is released: scripts/ADJUDICATION_INSTRUCTIONS.md sits beside the script it
# documents, because a reader replicating the adjudication needs it.
outreach/

# Clinician-adjudication files — PATIENT-LEVEL, never commit.
#   adjudication_key.json    maps case_id -> hadm_id / subject_id (400 real MIMIC ids)
#   adjudication_packet.csv  200 rows of demographics + labs
# The packet happens to be caught by the *.csv rule above; the key is JSON and was
# NOT caught, so it is named explicitly here. Both are regenerable from the seed and
# stratum targets recorded in 11_clinician_adjudication.py, which is what the paper
# promises instead of the files themselves.
adjudication_key.json
**/adjudication_key.json
adjudication_packet.csv
**/adjudication_packet.csv
# Returned clinician responses are patient-level judgements on those rows.
reviewer_*.csv
**/reviewer_*.csv

# Derived patient-level artifacts (trace bundles are DUA-covered too)
traces/
decision_traces/
cohorts/
auditnesy_mimic_out/
**/auditnesy_mimic_out/
audit_mimic_out/
**/audit_mimic_out/
audit_mimic_out*/
**/audit_mimic_out*/
audit_mimic_*/
**/audit_mimic_*/

# Models & runs
models/
runs/
*.pkl
*.pt
*.joblib

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Claude Code session / local tooling
.claude/

# Figure intermediates (regenerated from real results; keep scripts, not outputs)
figures/figdata/
figures/out/

# Venue template — third-party content, not ours to redistribute. Fetch it from
# the venue's own template page; ml4h2026_template_facts.json records what we
# needed from it (class options, required commands, autoloaded packages).
ml4h2026_template.tex

# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.bbl
*.blg
*.synctex.gz
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.toc

# Local bundles (rebuilt on demand; keep the sources, not the archives)
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.zip
.audit_bundle.tgz

# Internal working notes / revision-process artifacts — LOCAL ONLY, never pushed.
# These carry informal session narrative and revision-process detail; publishing
# them would expose material no reader needs and risks the double-blind review.
# Kept on disk so we retain the working context; excluded from the mirror.
PROJECT_STATUS.md
phase1_changelog.md
phase3_changelog.md
AuditNeSy_final_rapor.md
icd_label_citations.json

# pytest cache (pytest also drops its own .gitignore inside, but be explicit)
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
